        "work_observation": {"type":"record","settings":{"number":"001","territory":"work","status":"Working observation","version":"1.0","published":"19 August 2026","published_iso":"2026-08-19","reviewed":"19 August 2026","reviewed_iso":"2026-08-19","next_review":"By 19 February 2027, or earlier if evidence changes","author":"Mirellis Editorial","reviewer":"Internal editorial review — not external peer review","title":"Work can feel open after the scheduled workday has ended.","statement":"Some people describe unfinished thoughts, checking, physical activation or a missing next activity after work. Mirellis treats these as different situations rather than one inferred state.","evidence_basis":"The categories come from user-described difficulties and the current After Work pathway design. A small employee diary study is included only as external context for unfinished tasks and affective rumination.","limitation":"Mirellis has not conducted a representative prevalence study or clinical trial. The external study does not validate all four Mirellis categories and this record must not be used as a diagnosis.","source_1_citation":"Mirellis. Work → Recovery practical pathway.","source_1_url":"/pages/work-to-recovery","source_1_scope":"Internal provenance for the current categories and pathway design; not population evidence.","source_2_citation":"Syrek CJ, Weigelt O, Peifer C, Antoni CH. Zeigarnik's sleepless nights. Journal of Occupational Health Psychology. 2017;22(2):225–238. doi:10.1037/ocp0000031.","source_2_url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27101340/","source_2_scope":"Supports a bounded association between unfinished tasks, affective rumination and weekend sleep impairment in one diary study; not the full Mirellis model.","disclosure":"Mirellis designed and operates the After Work pathway. No external funding supported this record.","ai_disclosure":"AI assisted source organization and drafting. Mirellis Editorial checked the cited sources, limitations and final wording and remains accountable.","change_note":"Initial citation-ready version.","practice_label":"Use After Work privately","practice_url":"https://app.mirellis.in"}},
        "work_practice": {"type":"record","settings":{"number":"002","territory":"work","status":"Practice hypothesis","version":"1.0","published":"19 August 2026","published_iso":"2026-08-19","reviewed":"19 August 2026","reviewed_iso":"2026-08-19","next_review":"By 19 February 2027, or earlier if evidence changes","author":"Mirellis Editorial","reviewer":"Internal editorial review — not external peer review","title":"A visible return point may make unfinished work easier to leave for now.","statement":"The After Work practice asks a person to name one unfinished item, write the first visible action for tomorrow and close one work surface.","evidence_basis":"Smit reported a longitudinal sample of 103 employees pursuing 1,127 goals and an experimental manipulation in which planning incomplete goals improved detachment for a subgroup. A broader meta-analysis provides context on recovery experiences. Mirellis is testing a related, not identical, practice.","limitation":"Neither source tested the full Mirellis sequence. The current build does not prove improvement in recovery, sleep, stress or productivity, and the planning result should not be generalized to every user.","source_1_citation":"Smit BW. Successfully leaving work at work. Journal of Occupational and Organizational Psychology. 2016;89(3):493–514. doi:10.1111/joop.12137.","source_1_url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/joop.12137","source_1_scope":"Supports incomplete-goal and planning rationale in the reported samples; not efficacy of the exact Mirellis sequence.","source_2_citation":"Bennett AA, Bakker AB, Field JG. Recovery from work-related effort: A meta-analysis. Journal of Organizational Behavior. 2018;39:262–275. doi:10.1002/job.2217.","source_2_url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/job.2217","source_2_scope":"Provides broader context on psychological detachment and recovery outcomes across 54 independent samples; not a clinical trial of this practice.","disclosure":"Mirellis designed and operates the After Work practice. No external funding supported this record.","ai_disclosure":"AI assisted source organization and drafting. Mirellis Editorial checked the cited sources, limitations and final wording and remains accountable.","change_note":"Initial citation-ready version.","practice_label":"Try the practice","practice_url":"https://app.mirellis.in/?friction=unfinished"}},
